    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0467" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6639: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-03T15:00:00+01:00">May 3, 1934—3 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 3—8:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>241. Mayer’s 224, January 16, 2 p.m., Consulate’s 64, May 1, 2 p.m.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d276-f1"/> Haas<anchor n="43" xml:id="d276-f2"/> tells me that the
                    China Technical Committee will be called during the coming session of the
                    Council in the week beginning May 14 and that only the usual circular notice of
                    convocation will be sent out. As Department has made no comment of second
                    sentence of paragraph 1 of Mayer’s 224, January 16, 2 p.m., I assume that I
                    should attend the meeting in the capacity you prescribed on receiving notice of
                    the convocation. (Chinese-Japanese controversy.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d276-f1" n="42" xml:id="d276-f1-content">
                <p>For telegram No. 64, see <ref target="#pg150">p. 150</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d276-f2" n="43" xml:id="d276-f2-content">
                <p>Robert Haas (French), director of the League of Nations communications and
                    transit section.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
